  "title": ".mailmap, AUTHORS: map jaxlvl to Juan Carlos Valera a",
  "description": "## .mailmap, AUTHORS: map jaxlvl to Juan Carlos Valera and add CoAP-EAP dissector credit\n\n### Background\n\nThe bug fix MR !25547 (IEEE 802.15.4: Fix ccm_cbc_mac stack buffer underflow) was authored with the git identity `jaxlvl <160593716+jaxlvl@users.noreply.github.com>`. The identity was later corrected to `Juan Carlos Valera <juancarlosvalera999@gmail.com>` for the CoAP-EAP MR !25609.\n\nThe bug fix commit `d829fcf75c` permanently has `Author: jaxlvl`, `git shortlog` (and the `AUTHORS` file generated from it by `tools/generate_authors.py`) lists `jaxlvl` as a separate contributor, resulting in two entries for the same person.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`.mailmap`** — add an entry to map the old identity to the correct one:\n\nJuan Carlos Valera juancarlosvalera999@gmail.com jaxlvl 160593716+jaxlvl@users.noreply.github.com\n\n### Result\n\nAfter the next `[Automatic update]` regenerates `AUTHORS`:\n\n1. The `jaxlvl` entry is removed (consolidated via `.mailmap`).\n2. `Juan Carlos Valera` appears once in the Contributors section with the CoAP-EAP dissector credit, and is no longer duplicated in `= From git log =` (the script skips emails already listed in Contributors).\n\nAll the contributions (bug fix !25547 + CoAP-EAP dissector + test suite from !25609) are attributed to a single `Juan Carlos Valera` entry.",
  "state": "merged",
